   133	
   134	Test changes that the remediation needed:
   135	
   136	- aioresponses 0.7.9, the latest release, builds aiohttp responses without the `stream_writer` argument that aiohttp 3.14 requires (aio-libs/aiohttp#12815). `tests/conftest.py` gives this argument a default for the responses that aioresponses creates. Application code is not changed.
   137	- Seven tests create a `chroma` store through `VectorStoreFactory` with a mocked Chroma class. The factory uses the class only when chromadb can be imported, so these tests now skip when chromadb is not installed. Install the `vectorstores` extra to run them.
   138	
   139	## Container Build Check
   140	
   141	`scripts/verification/container_check.py --build` does these steps:
   142	
   143	1. **build:** `docker build` of the repository `Dockerfile`.
   144	2. **start:** `docker run` with no environment variables, so the image defaults apply: production mode, no credentials, no LLM key. The port is published only on `127.0.0.1:18000`.
   145	3. **ready:** poll `GET /health` until HTTP 200, for at most 300 seconds. The check stops at once when the container exits.
   146	4. **health:** `GET /health` and `GET /api/v1/health` answer HTTP 200 with a `status` field, and the image HEALTHCHECK reports `healthy` within 180 seconds. An image without a HEALTHCHECK fails.
   147	5. **auth:** `POST /api/v1/query` and `POST /api/v1/documents/reset` without credentials must answer HTTP 401.
   148	6. **user:** the effective UID of process 1 and of every other process in the container must not be 0. The image runs as `appuser` (UID 10001).
   149	
   150	The container is removed at the end, also after a failure. A second workflow step with `if: always()` removes every container with the label `tenant-rag-verification`. A failed check shows the failed step, the reason and the last 150 lines of the container log.
   151	
   152	## Verification Summary
   153	
   154	The `Verification Summary` job runs after all other checks, also when one of them fails. It writes a table (Check, Mode, Result, Findings/Details) to the job summary of the workflow run. Sections follow for failed Blocking Checks, the Security Regression Suite (manifest changes, failed and skipped tests), the Dependency Vulnerability Check (blocking advisories, accepted exceptions, non-blocking advisories), the Container Build Check (step results, runtime user, container log on failure) and the static analysis. A notice annotation gives the overall result.
   155	
   156	Each check also uploads its JSON report as an artifact named `verification-*`. GitHub keeps the artifacts for 14 days.
   157	
   158	## Run the checks locally
   159	
   160	```bash
   161	make verify             # every check; the container check needs Docker
   162	make verify-tests       # full test suite
   163	make verify-security    # Security Regression Suite
   164	make verify-static      # Ruff, MyPy and Bandit (report-only)
   165	make verify-deps        # Dependency Vulnerability Check
   166	make verify-container   # Container Build Check
   167	make security-manifest  # update the manifest after a security test change
   168	```
   169	
   170	The targets call `bash scripts/verify_pipeline.sh CHECK ...`, which uses the same tools and policies as CI. The Redis tests of the Security Regression Suite need a Redis server and `TEST_REDIS_URL=redis://localhost:6379/15`; without them these tests are skipped, and the suite fails. The reports and the summary go to `$TMPDIR/tenant-rag-verification-<timestamp>` (set `VERIFY_OUT_DIR` to change it). Set `PYTHON` to choose the interpreter.
   171	
   172	## Troubleshooting
   173	
   174	| Result | What to do |
   175	|---|---|
   176	| Security Regression Suite: security test(s) skipped | Find the skip reason in the job log or the Verification Summary. Provide the missing service or setting. Do not add `skip` or `xfail` to a security test. |
   177	| Security Regression Suite: tests not in the manifest | Run `make security-manifest` and commit the manifest. |
   178	| Security Regression Suite: tests missing | A security test was removed or renamed. Restore it, or update the manifest and explain the removal in the pull request. |
   179	| Dependency Vulnerability Check: blocking advisory | Upgrade the package to a fixed version. If there is no fix, remove the package or move it out of the default installation. An accepted exception is the last option. |
   180	| Dependency Vulnerability Check: error, OSV lookup failed | A network problem. Run the job again. |
   181	| Container Build Check: ready or health failed | Read the container log in the job log or the Verification Summary. |
   182	| Verification Summary: no report | The job of that check did not write a report. Open that job. |
   183	
   184	## Files
   185	
   186	- `.github/workflows/ci.yml`: the workflow
   187	- `scripts/verification/run_suite.py` and `scripts/verification/pytest_plugin/verification_outcomes.py`: test suite runner, Security Regression Suite gate and manifest handling
   188	- `scripts/verification/static_analysis.py`: Ruff, MyPy and Bandit checks
   189	- `scripts/verification/dependency_audit.py` and `scripts/verification/requirements-audit.txt`: Dependency Vulnerability Check
   190	- `scripts/verification/container_check.py`: Container Build Check
   191	- `scripts/verification/summary.py`: Verification Summary
   192	- `scripts/verify_pipeline.sh` and the `verify*` targets of the `Makefile`: local runs
   193	- `tests/security/suite_manifest.json`: security test list
   194	- `.github/dependency-audit-exceptions.json`: accepted exceptions
   195	- `tests/verification/`: tests of the pipeline tools
